  "details": "<p>The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: diocese The diocese covered northern and eastern Gaul and comprised a number of individual provinces, including Gallia Lugdunensis I, Gallia Lugdunensis II, Gallia Lugdunensis III, Gallia Lugdunensis IV (Senonia), Belgica I, Belgica II, Germania I, Germania II, Alpes Poenninae et Graiae and Maxima Sequanorum.</p>",
  "review_state": "published",
  "type": "FeatureCollection",
  "description": "The Diocese of Gaul was a diocese of the later Roman Empire.",
